WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.150
I am ranking the top 100 secrets most people
don’t know about One Piece. And if you want

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.380
to see if you are a true one piece expert,
keep watching all the way to number one to

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.969
see how many of these you actually know.

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:16.699
And we’ll start with our first mind-blowing
fact, which is that the anime completely skipped

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:21.689
the crucial first chapter of the manga until
episode four, leaving first time viewers unaware

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:23.500
of Luffy’s backstory.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.940
Which might sound crazy, but that’s just
the beginning because Nami, not Luffy, was

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:33.510
the first Straw Hat to appear in the anime,
looking fabulous while undercover on a random

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:34.670
passenger ship.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:40.129
However, there is absolutely no way she would
be able to sneak around undercover if Oda

00:00:40.129 --> 00:00:45.300
stuck with Nami’s original design. That’s
because in her first design she had both a

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:52.370
mechanical arm AND foot, plus she had this
totally badass battle ax. Personally, I’m

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.550
super curious how this would have changed
her journey in the story

00:00:55.550 --> 00:01:01.829
Though I bet you never realized that Nami
and Robin are the only crew members to betray

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:07.740
Luffy. Nami stole the ship and Robin framed
the crew for assassination. Seriously, don’t

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.049
mess with these women.

00:01:09.049 --> 00:01:15.340
What’s even more incredible is that many
of the most famous pirates in One Piece have

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:21.890
real world inspirations. Blackbeard and Whitebeard
were clearly inspired by the real Edward Teach,

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:28.470
also known as Blackbeard, but Roger’s famous
execution scene was inspired by a French pirate

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:33.829
who gave a famous puzzle during his execution.
Among many others, the silky smooth Alvida

00:01:33.829 --> 00:01:40.130
has a real life counterpart, as does Jewelry
Bonney and even Rocks D. Xebec, who was inspired

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:42.079
by a Brazilian pirate.

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:46.820
And from some of the most important pirates
in the story, let’s discuss some of the

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:52.810
most secret. This funny guy is Pandaman, a
character that Oda often draws in the background

00:01:52.810 --> 00:02:00.049
of chapters. While Pandaman may appear as
a simple gag, he possesses a full backstory,

00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:04.730
complete with a lover, a rival, and a gang
to whom he owes money.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:11.090
But Pandaman is not the only recurring gag
character. This is Manatomo, the traveling

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:16.330
carpenter who specializes in fixing broken
things. One of his notable repairs involved

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:21.190
the door to the bar, which had been broken
way back in chapter 1.

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:26.110
And we can’t forget about Sam, this bald
drunkard who sometimes shows up having had

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:30.010
a few too many drinks.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:37.640
Amazingly, Sanji and Brook actually had strikingly
similar introductions. Both wore a black suit

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:43.769
and held hot liquid. That was soup for Sanji
and Coffee for Brook. Plus they are the most

00:02:43.769 --> 00:02:48.400
perverted on the crew, so I am super curious
what other similarities we might learn in

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.400
the future.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:54.720
That’s not the only insane hidden fact about
Brook, because he is officially the only straw

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.830
hat to never meet either of Luffy’s brothers,
Sabo and Ace.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:04.730
Which might seem crazy but did you know that
among all the characters in one piece this

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:10.900
massive man, Urogue, embodies the essence
of a true pirate with his hobbies. These include

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.060
traveling, drinking, and, well... um lovemaking.
But who would want to— *Shakes* head, wave

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.390
hands No. No. I really don’t even want to
think about it.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:24.540
While Urogue may be getting plenty on the
side, the same can't be said for Kid and Killer.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:28.480
And that’s because they once shared a childhood
crush, but when they laughed at her for spilling

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:33.720
curry, she promptly beat the shit out of them.
So much for punk rock love.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:38.840
But the same can’t be said for Blackbeard
because these two ladies we see hanging off

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:44.760
him are called Tori and Maki, which if you
put them together is Torimaki. And in Japanese

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:51.849
this roughly translates to gold digger, who
is a woman who sleeps with men for their money.

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:58.750
On the other hand, one pirate who’s definitely
not getting the ladies, is this cat-loving

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:03.659
fake butler. And that’s because Oda has
officially confirmed that these weird little

00:04:03.659 --> 00:04:08.319
golden blobs on his jacket are actually meant
to be poop.

00:04:08.319 --> 00:04:13.530
However, make fun of him at your own risk
because he backs a serious punch. In fact,

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:18.549
you might not know that the former Marine
Captain Morgan once tried to capture Kuro,

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:24.620
but the cat pirate broke his jaw which is
why Morgan has this metal mouthpiece.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:30.530
As unlikely as it may sound, Kuro isn’t
even the weirdest member of his crew. That

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:35.870
honor belongs to Jango, who has this weird
stem looking facial hair. But it turns out

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:42.120
that this is not even hair. Instead Oda has
confirmed that it is the stem of a mushroom

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.530
that somehow started growing on Jango’s
face

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:55.690
Amazingly, what is not fake is this god damn
luxurious facial hair. However, what you might

00:04:55.690 --> 00:05:00.620
not know about Gol D. Roger’s famous mustache
is that Oda originally planned for this to

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:06.030
just be super long nose hairs. Yikes. Kinda
gross.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:10.350
And while Ace didn’t inherit his father’s
impressive facial hair, he is actually the

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:15.830
only known character in the story to reject
an invitation to join the World Government’s

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:16.830
Warlords.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:21.100
Now, have you ever wanted to have Luffy’s
courage? Or magically learn his ability to

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:26.550
never get nervous? Well, you might want to
reconsider after you hear THIS. According

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:31.910
to the author of One Piece, Luffy is only
like this because he is a complete idiot who

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.680
doesn’t know any better.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:39.280
But okay, okay, even if you knew that fact,
did you know that we almost had THIS in the

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:43.330
story. That’s right, Sanji was originally
planned to be called Naruto, but since the

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:48.960
Naruto that we all know and love was becoming
its own popular manga at the time, Eiichiro

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:53.000
Oda, the author of One Piece, decided to change
his name to avoid confusion.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:06:00.280
Alright, so far that’s 20 facts. Did you
know all of those? Well even if you did, I

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.750
bet you didn’t know that…

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:08.220
The pirate empress Boa Hancock actually appeared
on a cover of Shonen Jump all the way back

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:15.900
in 1999? That’s nine whole years before
her introduction in the story.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:21.000
You might not know she’s not even the only
character to appear in a magazine. That’s

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:26.720
because in chapter 762, Law’s mentor, Corazon
is reading a newspaper that shows the Warlord

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:32.120
Crocodile. Apparently this article was praising
Crocodile’s heroism for hunting down pirates

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:36.259
during his early years as a Warlord.

00:06:36.259 --> 00:06:41.370
While the incredible recent events of Cross
Guild have Crocodile teaming up with the world’s

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:46.620
strongest swordsman, here is a little known
fact about Mihawk. Apparently, he was famous

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:51.949
even before Roger’s execution began the
Great Pirate Era. Which makes me super curious

00:06:51.949 --> 00:06:57.599
what he was doing during all this time. And
as we discussed in a recent chapter review,

00:06:57.599 --> 00:07:02.039
it's actually possible that he might have
been working for the Celestial Dragons.

00:07:02.039 --> 00:07:08.669
This next fact goes back even before the Celestial
Dragons existed. And that’s because the

00:07:08.669 --> 00:07:14.039
earliest event that we have an official date
for is the Golden Age of Shandora, which was

00:07:14.039 --> 00:07:24.860
stated to occur during the early 402 which
is about 1100 years before the current story.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:29.270
This next fact is just as incredibly old.
And that’s because the animal mink tribe

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:35.880
has lived on the back of this giant elephant
for over 1000 years, which means that they

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:38.690
were outcasts even before the void century.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:43.460
However, would you believe me if I told you
there is an even more secret and mysterious

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:49.090
elephant than Zunesha? Listen to this. The
new warden of impel down has a strange obsession

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:54.740
with underwear? In fact, Oda shows us his
collection in a question corner, including

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.660
this one called, Mr. Elephant. eh-hem *starts
typing, whispers off screen*. Where can I

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:01.580
get one of those… oh, right, back to the
video.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:07.810
What’s even crazier though is that Shanks
has been putting his own Mr. Elephant to work.

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:16.000
In the cover of chapter 614, we see the bartender
Makino holding this young child. When asked

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:22.080
who the father of this child was, Oda simply
replied that it is probably “that man”,

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:26.629
which strongly suggests that it is Shanks,
since the Red Hair captain visits her bar

00:08:26.629 --> 00:08:31.039
often, as we see in the very first chapter.

00:08:31.039 --> 00:08:35.599
What’s even more interesting is that the
Straw Hat's ship, the Thousand Sunny, hides

00:08:35.599 --> 00:08:43.779
a locked freezer with a passcode? Only Sanji,
Nami, and Robin know the combination, which

00:08:43.779 --> 00:08:49.310
is based on their birthdays.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:55.310
The Thousand Sunny also boasts a surprising
library. Every Straw Hat pirate, except Luffy,

00:08:55.310 --> 00:09:00.620
has at least one book in the collection. Even
Zoro enjoys looking at books about swords

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.900
and Jinbe likely added books about the seas
after joining.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:11.779
On the other hand, do you want to know the
most disgusting fact about the ship? The men

00:09:11.779 --> 00:09:18.430
rarely use the toilet. Instead, they do their
business off the side. Which was actually

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:23.570
common for sailors, and many boats had "crap
lines" on the ship to help sailors avoid falling

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.120
overboard.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:33.830
Now, instead of food going out, let’s talk
about one man who knows how to appreciate

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:39.800
his comfort food. That’s because this guy,
Vergo, finds comfort in a daily breakfast

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:44.829
routine of hamburgers, fries, and a strawberry
milkshake.

00:09:44.829 --> 00:09:52.720
But one thing he apparently won’t eat is
devil fruits, because he is the only one of

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:56.650
Doflamingo’s officers to not have eaten
a devil fruit.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:04.040
Next is a fact you’ll definitely only know
if you are a die hard Sanji fan. That’s

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:09.170
because over the entire 1000 plus chapters,
Zoro has never called Sanji by his proper

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:14.890
name in the original Japanese manga.

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:21.260
And while many fans assume that the two hate
each other, they actually care about each

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:26.399
other quite a lot. They have proven that they
will even risk their lives to save the others,

00:10:26.399 --> 00:10:28.790
such as in Thriller Bark and in Wano.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:34.560
Which means that this next fact could have
completely ruined the best bromance in manga.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:41.710
That’s because this fierce rivalry almost
never existed. Originally, Zoro was planned

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:50.340
to be a simple bodyguard for Buggy, meaning
he would have been left behind long ago.

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:57.060
Though honestly I would love to see how the
story would change if some of Oda’s craziest

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:01.310
ideas were included, so make sure to subscribe
to the channel if you want to see a future

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:02.790
video on that topic.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:09.310
This next fact shows us just how sneaky Oda
can be. That’s because Oda has included

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:16.570
his name and the title of the story on various
books throughout the story, including episode

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:20.870
21, 70, and 278.

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:25.350
While you might be frantically looking back
through the story now, stick around because

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:30.260
you won’t believe these incredible facts
about Dressrosa that you probably missed.

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:35.589
Like, did you know that this samurai never
actually received a bounty from the Doflamingo

00:11:35.589 --> 00:11:42.490
family. And that’s because Kanjuro was actually
working for Doflamingo’s bosses all along.

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:51.300
In Dressrosa, we also meet the Tontatta dwarves,
who live on Greenbit. But did you ever realize

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:56.680
that the famous explorer Noland, who we met
in the Skypiea flashback actually found the

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:00.839
dwarves during his travels.

00:12:00.839 --> 00:12:05.860
Even if you knew that, I bet you never realized
that this snow harpy lady was actually the

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:11.830
very first female character to die in the
main story, not including flashbacks.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:18.880
Here is another unbelievable fact about other
Logia fruit users. Every one of these powerhouses

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:25.560
that were introduced before the time skip,
was present during the war at Marineford,

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:27.940
except the lightning fruit user, Enel.

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:32.519
What’s even crazier about Enel is that he
was actually the first major antagonist who

00:12:32.519 --> 00:12:36.460
was not either a pirate or a marine.

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:41.589
Putting slim shady aside, out of all of these
extremely powerful devil fruit users at Marineford,

00:12:41.589 --> 00:12:47.000
the very first one introduced into the story
was Smoker, who was also the first marine

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:50.280
shown with a devil fruit all the way back
in Logue Town.

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:55.279
But while we wait and pray for another epic
clash like Marineford in the future, we do

00:12:55.279 --> 00:13:00.810
already know the winner of one of Usopp’s
most important battles in the story. And that’s

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:10.660
because Usopp’s nose is confirmed to be
just slightly longer than this guy’s.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:15.630
Speaking of appearances, have you ever noticed
that these three brothers all have incredibly

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:22.290
unique hats? I mean come on, why doesn’t
anyone else in the story have such epic headwear?

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:26.501
While it’s hard to believe that Luffy has
the best hat game in the entire series, it's

00:13:26.501 --> 00:13:33.110
worth noting that Zoro, Sanji, and Nami each
hold a different important title—they are

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:37.630
the only ones in their twenties among the
crew. Zoro and Sanji are twenty-one, while

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:42.540
Nami adds her youthful charm at twenty.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:47.660
Although Zoro is in that honorable club, Zoro
also stands alone as the only member of the

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:54.680
Worst Generation without a devil fruit. This
guy also never had a devil fruit, until he

00:13:54.680 --> 00:14:03.209
was technically forced to eat an artificial
devil fruit during the Wano arc.

00:14:03.209 --> 00:14:07.829
Shifting gears to a completely different setting,
let's delve into some mind-blowing revelations

00:14:07.829 --> 00:14:15.100
about the prisoners residing in the underwater
prison, Impel Down. First is that Mr. 2 somehow

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:20.720
survived his fight with the venomous warden
and is now the new ruler of New Kama land.

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:26.160
What’s even crazier is that while Mr. 2
is still in prison, another former enemy was

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:32.240
once set free. That would be the fishman Arlong,
who is the only individual we know to have

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:37.509
ever been released from Impel Down. This was
only allowed because Jinbe agreed to join

00:14:37.509 --> 00:14:43.040
the Warlords and demanded that his fishman
brother be released.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:50.610
Then we have this insanely strong former prisoner,
Daz Bones, who is actually the only confirmed

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.380
bounty hunter to have ever eaten a devil fruit

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:59.170
However, during the chaos of Impel Down Daz
Bones escaped with Luffy and went to fight

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:04.310
a Marineford. But did you know that the war
at Marineford introduced the first two Mythical

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:10.150
Zoan fruits into the story. During this battle
we saw not only Marco’s Mythical Phoenix

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:17.190
fruit, but also the fleet admiral Sengoku’s
Mythical Golden Buddha fruit.

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:22.279
Still feeling great about your random one
piece knowledge? Or are you just along for

00:15:22.279 --> 00:15:27.399
the ride at this point? Either way, let’s
jump into the second half of our Hidden Facts

00:15:27.399 --> 00:15:28.930
Ranking!

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:35.069
Going right back to insanely overpowered devil
fruits, we now have nine mythical Zoans in

00:15:35.069 --> 00:15:40.460
the story. But you might not realize that
a shocking six of them were revealed during

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:45.779
the Wano arc. Those nine are the Yamata no
Orochi fruit, Kaido’s Mythical fish fruit,

00:15:45.779 --> 00:15:51.139
this shape-shifting Onyudo fruit, Caterina
Devon’s Nine-tailed fox fruit, Yamato’s

00:15:51.139 --> 00:15:55.160
wolf deity fruit, and, of course, Luffy’s
Nika fruit.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:16:00.800
That means that the only other Mythical Zoan
revealed outside of Marineford and Wano is

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:06.620
the Mythical Peagasus fruit, which was recently
shown by the horse Stronger during the Egghead

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:07.620
Island ar.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:12.480
Though all of these mythical Zoans are absurdly
powerful, you might not have realized that

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:18.480
basically none of them are as strong as Akainu’s
magma fruit. In fact, did you know that Akainu’s

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:24.060
powers are so strong that he was able to destroy
one of Aokiji’s legs and leave him with

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:29.750
burns all along his arm?

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:40.040
Now, let's shift our focus to another mind-blowing
example of foreshadowing. Did you know that

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:45.839
in the anime, Zoro gave Luffy a striking X
scar on his chest that was incredibly similar

00:16:45.839 --> 00:16:53.161
to the scar he received from this magma fist.
Talk about incredible foreshadowing, even

00:16:53.161 --> 00:16:54.950
in a filler episode!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:17:00.709
Speaking of foreshadowing, did you know that
Sanji gave himself the nickname “Mr. Prince”

00:17:00.709 --> 00:17:06.680
in Little Garden it was actually foreshadowing
Sanji’s true lineage as a prince of the

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:07.680
Vinsmoke

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:13.829
While it took over six hundred chapters for
that foreshadowing to pay off, Jinbe is also

00:17:13.829 --> 00:17:18.890
another example of Oda’s incredible long
term planning. That’s because he was directly

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:26.140
mentioned way back in chapter 69, but was
not officially revealed in the manga until

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:29.470
a staggering 459 chapters later.

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:34.700
On the other hand, Robin burst in without
any invitation at all. In fact, she is the

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:39.549
only straw hat who Luffy did not invite to
join the crew.

00:17:39.549 --> 00:17:44.610
Now, do you know who he said are the hardest
characters to draw? That would be the most

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:50.240
beautiful woman in the world, Hancock, and
also the mermaid princess Shirahosi. Hmm,

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:52.500
I wonder why?

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:57.429
Sticking with our favorite mangaka, Oda once
shared that if he could choose a Devil Fruit

00:17:57.429 --> 00:18:04.080
power, he'd opt for Robin's Hana Hana no Mi
so that he could have more hands to draw the

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:11.140
story. Personally, I’d probably choose the
Phoenix fruit, but Robin’s is cool too.

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:16.700
Now let’s get to some truly unbelievable
facts about the world of One Piece and it’s

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:21.919
creators. First, did you know that One Piece
was only supposed to last for five years.

00:18:21.919 --> 00:18:23.659
*chuckles*, whoops.

00:18:23.659 --> 00:18:30.090
On top of that, the Warlords were never planned
to exist in the story. Oda had originally

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:35.760
only planned for Luffy to only fight the Yonko.
So goodbye, to all of you chumps.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:42.030
That’s not even all of the major factions
who randomly became a part of the story, because

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:48.059
Oda famously made up the entire group of Supernova
pirates at the very last minute before they

00:18:48.059 --> 00:18:51.890
appeared in the story.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:57.429
Which is hard to believe, but did you also
know that Nami is the only straw hat to invite

00:18:57.429 --> 00:19:04.890
someone else onto the crew before Luffy did.
This happened in chapter 140, she asked Chopper

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:08.049
if he wanted to come along on their grand
adventure.

00:19:08.049 --> 00:19:15.830
And while the Chopper we know and love is
an adorable reindeer, Oda almost gave us THIS

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:22.740
SHOCKING DESIGN. Yeah, so this cuddly reindeer
was almost a chain smoking Zebra-reindeer

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:30.240
hybrid instead. It’s actually pretty incredible
how much some of the crew changed from their

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:31.680
original designs.

00:19:31.680 --> 00:19:36.850
Similarly, did you know that Chopper's current
design was inspired by the most famous reindeer

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:43.380
of all?&nbsp;Chopper just has a blue nose instead
of red, and his birthday is even on Christmas

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:44.380
eve.

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:48.760
We all know Chopper’s goal is to save lives,
but he isn’t the only merciful member of

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:55.799
the crew. Surprisingly, Luffy has never actually
killed a major opponent in the series – except

00:19:55.799 --> 00:20:01.760
maybe Kaido, but that part is a little unclear.
But this is actually an intentional choice

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:07.990
because Oda believes that crushing someone’s
dream is a fate even worse than death.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:14.310
However, that’s far from the only major
hidden secret Luffy has up his sleeve. In

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:18.289
fact, we all know that Luffy wants to become
king of the pirates, but that’s actually

00:20:18.289 --> 00:20:24.730
only one part of his true dream. However,
we're left in the dark about this secret wish,

00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:30.380
but every time he has told someone in the
story, they usually think it is quite amusing.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:38.429
Now, I want you to pause and think about this:
what is the most disturbing scene in all of

00:20:38.429 --> 00:20:44.440
One Piece? Do you have it in mind? Well, you’re
probably wrong. That’s because of this scene

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:50.600
during the final battle of the One Piece movie:
Baron Omatsuri and the Secret Island. And

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:57.150
I won’t spoil it for you, but it was so
awful that it nearly wiped out the entire

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:58.150
crew.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:01.919
If that’s hard to think about, just wait
because that’s not even the most tragic

00:21:01.919 --> 00:21:07.730
fact about One Piece. A number of the anime
voice actors have passed away during the run

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:14.280
of the show. These include voice actors for
Jinbe, Rayleigh, Mihawk, Sengoku, Smoker,

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:18.990
Gol D. Roger, and a few more. And it genuinely
makes me sad that they’ll never get to reach

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:21.049
the end of Luffy’s journey.

00:21:21.049 --> 00:21:26.820
Unsurprisingly, Oda is just as emotionally
invested in the story as we are. In fact,

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:32.710
he often finds himself moved to tears by his
own scenes such as bidding a tearful farewell

00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:37.860
to the beloved Going Merry or witnessing Vivi's
desperate pleas for peace in Alabasta.

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:43.260
Now let’s stick with Luffy a little longer
with some quick hitter hidden facts. Ready?

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:47.159
Let’s go. Did you know that Luffy only bathes
once a week?

00:21:47.159 --> 00:21:50.429
Or that he is the youngest member of the worst
generation of pirates

00:21:50.429 --> 00:21:56.409
And that Luffy has ranked first in every single
One Piece popularity poll?

00:21:56.409 --> 00:22:02.779
Plus another completely bizarre fact is that
Luffy, Usopp, and Sanji all claim to have

00:22:02.779 --> 00:22:06.530
never been sick, so they don’t actually
know what it feels like to have those cold

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:11.429
symptoms. I mean, Luffy’s been poisoned
plenty of times, and he’s always survived,

00:22:11.429 --> 00:22:16.780
so maybe he just has a ridiculous immune system.
As for Sanji and Usopp, well, that’s a bit

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:20.720
more debatable if they are telling the truth
or just trying to show off.

00:22:20.720 --> 00:22:25.870
Now, let's rewind to Luffy's childhood, where
he befriends Sabo in the class-divided Goa

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:31.940
Kingdom. But the surprise comes when their
paths cross again in Dressrosa, which is yet

00:22:31.940 --> 00:22:37.490
another kingdom plagued by class divisions
with a peculiar twist—its lower-tier citizens

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:40.190
are transformed into literal toys.

00:22:40.190 --> 00:22:44.559
In addition, just like when Luffy smashed
Doflamingo into the ground, did you know that

00:22:44.559 --> 00:22:50.409
there is one thing that ALWAYS happens after
Luffy takes down a major antagonist? No, it’s

00:22:50.409 --> 00:22:56.780
not a party, but we do always see Luffy crack
that characteristic big grin within one or

00:22:56.780 --> 00:23:01.950
two chapters after taking down the big bad
guy.

00:23:01.950 --> 00:23:08.340
What’s even crazier though is that Luffy
certainly deserves those smiles, because he

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:13.039
and the rest of the straw hats have all lost
someone significant to them in their past.

00:23:13.039 --> 00:23:19.640
Parents, mentors, brothers. No one is safe
from the Straw Hat’s pasts.

00:23:19.640 --> 00:23:24.771
As strange as that is, did you know that the
Marines aren’t the only branch of the World

00:23:24.771 --> 00:23:30.090
Government’s Military? As we can see on
this wanted poster drawn by Oda, there is

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:40.500
clearly Coast Guard written instead of Marines.

00:23:40.500 --> 00:23:45.390
So since the Coast Guard does exist, I wonder
if they have a special dish they eat every

00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:50.960
week? Because apparently, the Marines’ Friday
tradition is to eat a very special dish called

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:53.860
Marine Curry.

00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:59.380
Even that is not as surprising as Robin’s
other job on the Straw Hat crew. That’s

00:23:59.380 --> 00:24:04.809
because Robin is also one of the straw hat’s
hair stylists. We learned this in a question

00:24:04.809 --> 00:24:09.460
corner when Oda said that Usopp and Robin
cut the crew’s hair, and then after the

00:24:09.460 --> 00:24:12.970
timeskip, Sanji was added to the hair cutting
team.

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:16.279
And much to everyone’s surprise, the World
Government was actually more desperate to

00:24:16.279 --> 00:24:21.650
get their hands on one particular object than
they were about capturing fearsome pirates

00:24:21.650 --> 00:24:27.059
like Kaido, Shanks, and Big Mom. This object
is the Ope Ope no Mi, and they were willing

00:24:27.059 --> 00:24:35.070
to pay a staggering 5 billion berries to recover
it before Law consumed its powers.

00:24:35.070 --> 00:24:40.051
Shifting from one of the most valuable things
in the story, let’s meet the weakest. Do

00:24:40.051 --> 00:24:46.080
you know who it is? Well, that would be Batchee,
the small cricket that was unfairly squished

00:24:46.080 --> 00:24:47.970
by this marine during the Baratie arc.

00:24:47.970 --> 00:24:52.840
This brings us to a few more incredible facts
about the straw hats themselves. Oda once

00:24:52.840 --> 00:24:57.890
confirmed that Nami was the third smartest
character we had seen in the East Blue, only

00:24:57.890 --> 00:25:02.780
behind these two. However, with Nami's growth
throughout the story, it wouldn't be surprising

00:25:02.780 --> 00:25:05.830
if her ranking has improved since then

00:25:05.830 --> 00:25:11.539
Here's a fact straight from the author himself:
Usopp will forever hold the title of the weakest

00:25:11.539 --> 00:25:17.360
Straw Hat, regardless of who joins the crew.
This distinction arises from Usopp's relatability

00:25:17.360 --> 00:25:22.210
to normal people, while his crewmates all
have extraordinary powers

00:25:22.210 --> 00:25:28.490
What very few people actually know is that
Usopp actually has his own hidden superpower?

00:25:28.490 --> 00:25:33.799
That’s because many of Usopp’s lies from
the very first chapter have actually come

00:25:33.799 --> 00:25:39.660
true. He found the emerald city, met a mole,
encountered the three headed dog, fought a

00:25:39.660 --> 00:25:42.440
dragon, and even survived a giant goldfish.

00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:49.190
But no Usopp fact is more important than his
birthday, which is actually on April 1st.

00:25:49.190 --> 00:25:55.110
This is hilariously appropriate because April
1st is April Fools' Day in many parts of the

00:25:55.110 --> 00:25:56.110
world.

00:25:56.110 --> 00:26:01.899
What not a joke is the real-life inspiration
behind the revolutionary army.Dragon's ship,

00:26:01.899 --> 00:26:07.520
as the Wind Granma, is based on a historical
yacht that played a significant role in transporting

00:26:07.520 --> 00:26:14.140
rebel soldiers aiming to overthrow a former
Cuban president. Sound familiar?

00:26:14.140 --> 00:26:19.020
The most heart-warming fact about Robin is
that before Enies Lobby, she did not call

00:26:19.020 --> 00:26:24.100
any of the straw hat crewmates by name. Instead
she called them by titles such as “Navigator”

00:26:24.100 --> 00:26:30.260
or “Cook”. And this was because she never
let herself be fully accepted as a true member

00:26:30.260 --> 00:26:34.720
of the crew until the Straw Hats saved her
from the World Government

00:26:34.720 --> 00:26:40.090
Just like Robin, even Oda needs to feel accepted
sometimes. And one important milestone for

00:26:40.090 --> 00:26:45.830
him was passing the number of chapters in
the legendary original Dragon Ball manga.

00:26:45.830 --> 00:26:52.299
This occurred in chapter 519, and to mark
the achievement, Oda included special shading

00:26:52.299 --> 00:26:54.880
and tone on the cover page.

00:26:54.880 --> 00:27:00.850
But one fact that is almost too shocking to
believe is about Sanji’s eyebrows. And that’s

00:27:00.850 --> 00:27:04.820
because&nbsp; when Sanji actually used the super
powered raid suit during his fight in Wano,

00:27:04.820 --> 00:27:12.429
his curly eyebrows literally changed direction
to match his brothers. This was hugely symbolic

00:27:12.429 --> 00:27:16.840
because Sanji’s eyebrows have always been
different to show that he is more human than

00:27:16.840 --> 00:27:22.460
his emotionless brothers. However, once Sanji
rejected the raid suit later on, his eyebrows

00:27:22.460 --> 00:27:24.590
turned back to their normal form.

00:27:24.590 --> 00:27:35.149
And now into the top 10 most secret, crazy,
astonishing facts about One Piece.

00:27:35.149 --> 00:27:40.720
We all know that chapter 1 is also the moment
where Luffy stabs himself which results in

00:27:40.720 --> 00:27:47.680
his famous scar. But did you ever notice that
Luffy’s Grandpa and Father also have noticeable

00:27:47.680 --> 00:27:54.090
marks on the left side of their faces. Garp
has a scar and Dragon has this tattoo. Surely

00:27:54.090 --> 00:27:59.320
this must have some meeting, and I’ll give
you another hint about its true importance

00:27:59.320 --> 00:28:02.580
in the very last fact of this video.

00:28:02.580 --> 00:28:09.090
While this is one crazy family, it is nowhere
near as insane as the biggest family in the

00:28:09.090 --> 00:28:17.120
story. That’s because Big Mom has been somehow
giving birth for 42 STRAIGHT YEARS! She has

00:28:17.120 --> 00:28:25.159
had 43 husbands which have produced 39 daughters
and 46 sons. Yeesh. Somewhere my Mom is in

00:28:25.159 --> 00:28:33.600
pain just thinking about 46 little Manu’s
running around the house.

00:28:33.600 --> 00:28:38.429
What you didn’t know about Big Mom's strongest
son, Katakuri, is that he’s also officially

00:28:38.429 --> 00:28:44.160
the biggest donut lover in the entire story.
In fact, he may hold the record for the most

00:28:44.160 --> 00:28:49.690
donuts consumed in a row, a feat that even
Garp attempted to beat by devouring a staggering

00:28:49.690 --> 00:28:57.880
834 of them. Umm, hello, where can I sign
up for this donut-eating championship? Custard

00:28:57.880 --> 00:28:59.700
Cream for me, please.

00:28:59.700 --> 00:29:05.529
Now, do you know which of the most iconic
scenes of the story was almost erased by a

00:29:05.529 --> 00:29:12.070
real-life natural disaster? That would be
this one. That’s right, we almost never

00:29:12.070 --> 00:29:18.470
got to see Blackbeard show off his new powers
in the anime because during this time, a massive

00:29:18.470 --> 00:29:25.460
earthquake triggered a tsunami that caused
immense damage in Japan. This scene from the

00:29:25.460 --> 00:29:31.320
anime aired only weeks before this disaster,
but I have to wonder if they would have taken

00:29:31.320 --> 00:29:35.740
it out had the tsunami had happened before
the scene in the anime.

00:29:35.740 --> 00:29:41.399
At number six, did you know there is one One
Piece fan who absolutely knew how One Piece

00:29:41.399 --> 00:29:46.870
ended? That’s because one young fan who
had lung cancer asked the Make a Wish Foundation

00:29:46.870 --> 00:29:52.549
if he could learn the end of One Piece. So
Oda agreed to fulfill the kids last request,

00:29:52.549 --> 00:29:59.011
and revealed how One Piece would end to the
one fan alone. So thank you Oda-sensei, for

00:29:59.011 --> 00:30:02.559
granting wishes with your incredible story.

00:30:02.559 --> 00:30:08.250
What’s crazy about One Piece is that sometimes
it is super easy to forget the actual timeline

00:30:08.250 --> 00:30:17.159
of the story. Like, can you believe that the
first half of the story unfolded within a

00:30:17.159 --> 00:30:25.500
mere four months in the One Piece world? So
Luffy went from this to this in the same time

00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:32.150
it takes to complete a semester of school.
Wow, what are we doing with our lives…

00:30:32.150 --> 00:30:37.800
And did you know that Sabo might actually
have been revealed back in chapter 98. That’s

00:30:37.800 --> 00:30:43.820
because right here we can see a character
in a black suit and hat who looks just like

00:30:43.820 --> 00:30:50.000
Sabo. He shows up again right here. And it
would make sense that Sabo is here because

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:55.909
Dragon, the leader of the revolutionary army,
also shows up to save Luffy.

00:30:55.909 --> 00:31:01.130
Another shocking fact is that two of the most
god-like, and popular, characters in the story

00:31:01.130 --> 00:31:07.190
have never actually met. If you don’t know,
I’m talking about the god of lies, Usopp,

00:31:07.190 --> 00:31:11.279
and the hero who fails his way to the top,
Buggy the Clown.

00:31:11.279 --> 00:31:17.020
Now, this next fact is going to make you completely
rethink who the strongest straw hat is. And

00:31:17.020 --> 00:31:23.270
that’s because Nico Robin had an even higher
bounty than the strongest creature in the

00:31:23.270 --> 00:31:25.900
world, Kaido, when they were both the same
age as children.

00:31:25.900 --> 00:31:31.429
That means for the absolute most insane hidden
fact in all of one piece is the secret symbol

00:31:31.429 --> 00:31:36.269
of the left eye. Throughout the story, Oda
has drawn many characters with their left

00:31:36.269 --> 00:31:41.389
eye closed including these volume covers.
The symbol also shows up on the map of Jaya

00:31:41.389 --> 00:31:47.190
and even on this abstract painting in Dressrosa.
And I bet you can’t even imagine just how

00:31:47.190 --> 00:31:51.780
much this symbol reveals about where to find
Laugh Tale, what the ancient kingdom was,

00:31:51.780 --> 00:31:53.880
and how the future of the story will go.

00:31:53.880 --> 00:31:59.470
And just to top it off, here is one last bonus
fact. Did you know who is the only character

00:31:59.470 --> 00:32:05.309
who rejected the chance to join both Gol D.
Roger and the Straw Hat crew as a kid? That

00:32:05.309 --> 00:32:11.660
would be Franky, and if you want to know exactly
why he initially rejected both crews, you

00:32:11.660 --> 00:32:14.100
can watch this video right here.

00:32:14.100 --> 00:32:15.170
Shanks for Watching

